    "faq_WMzaQr": {
      "type": "faq",
      "blocks": {
        "question_EXaq3R": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is an electric commuter bike?",
            "answer": "<p>An electric commuter bike is an e‑bike designed for everyday trips like riding to work, school, or around the city. It combines a traditional bike with a motor and battery to give you extra help when you pedal, so you can ride farther, climb hills more easily, and arrive feeling fresher.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_MANd4H": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What should I consider before buying a commuter e-bike?",
            "answer": "<p>When choosing a commuter e-bike, think about three key things: how far you ride, how it feels to ride, and how safe it is.<br/><br/>Range: Choose a battery that can comfortably cover your round-trip commute distance, including small detours, so you do not worry about running out of power.<br/><br/>Comfort: Choose a commuter electric bike with a step-thru frame, front suspension fork, suspension seatpost, and city tires to make it easier to get on and off, absorb bumps, and reduce fatigue on your daily rides.<br/><br/>Safety: Choose a model with bright front and rear lights, reliable brakes with strong stopping power, and a clear display so you can see and be seen in traffic and always know your speed and battery level.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_iCnf4V": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How do I ride? Do I have to pedal?",
            "answer": "<p>You ride a Maxfoot e-bike like a regular bicycle, with the motor adding pedal assist to make each ride easier. The thumb throttle also lets you move without pedaling when you want a quick boost or a short rest.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_XQAhqt": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "How far can it go on a full charge?",
            "answer": "<p>Range will always depend on factors like rider weight, terrain, wind, and how much pedal assist or throttle you use.<br/>Under typical city riding conditions, this Maxfoot commuter e-bike can travel up to 50 miles on a single charge when using lower assist levels and active pedaling.<br/>If you use higher assist levels or the throttle more often, the actual range will be shorter, but still enough for most daily commutes and errands.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_KwCzBK": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What maintenance does a commuter e-bike need?",
            "answer": "<p>The most important part of maintaining your commuter e-bike is taking care of the battery.<br/>Always use the original charger, avoid letting the battery sit completely empty for long periods, and try to charge it in a cool, dry place at room temperature.<br/><br/>If you will not ride for a while, store the battery around half charge and check it every few weeks to top it up, rather than leaving it fully drained or fully charged all the time.<br/><br/>Along with regular checks on your brakes, tires, and chain, these simple habits help your Maxfoot commuter e-bike stay safe, reliable, and keep its range for longer.</p>"
          }
        },
        "question_KHAXbj": {
          "type": "question",
          "settings": {
            "question": "What is the warranty on Maxfoot bike?",
            "answer": "<p>MAXFOOT electric bikes come with a 1-year limited warranty on electrical parts and 2 years of technical support warranty for most mechanical parts. Click here to view the full warranty policy.</p>"
